{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>And a tenth of fine flour.</b> A tenth of an ephah — forty-three and a fifth eggs." "<b>Beaten oil.</b> 'Beaten' is stated not as an obligation but as a fitness requirement. For since it says 'beaten for the luminary' — which implies for the luminary and not for the meal-offerings — one might think to disqualify it for meal-offerings. Therefore Scripture says 'beaten' here, and the meaning is not 'beaten for the luminary' but to exclude meal-offerings, which do not require beating — even grinding in a mill is valid for them (Menachot 6)." "<b>A quarter of a hin.</b> Three logs." "<b>And a drink-offering.</b> Into the bowls, as we learned in tractate Sukkah (48) — two silver bowls were at the top of the altar, perforated like two thin snouts. He pours the wine into them and it trickles out through the snout and falls onto the top of the altar, and from there it descends to the drain — in the altar of the eternal house; and on the bronze altar it descends from the altar to the ground."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:40.001883340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}